6.3. The Authority has no obligation to accept any application or award a grant funding if it determines the application fails the background checks.

6.4. Applications for permanent infrastructure, biosecurity capital items and the SPHN advice package will only be granted funding where these will be used to support tree health actions (felling, treatment, extraction, restocking).

6.5. Applicants issued with a Statutory Plant Health Notice (SPHN) must not undertake funded activities that conflict with the conditions of an SPHN.

6.6. Where an enforcement action is brought by the Authority against a grant recipient or any of its representatives for non-compliance with FC regulations, the grant payment may be withheld.

6.7. The Grant Recipient is required to submit a Biosecurity Management Plan to The Authority prior to the commencement of any Grant Funded Activities, to ensure that good biosecurity practice is upheld.
